      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town's charter on May 11, 1749 makes it Virginia's oldest continuously chartered town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dumfries%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1690 Richard Gibson built a gristmill on Quantico Creek, marking the town's earliest industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dumfries%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During the Revolutionary War, Dumfries served as a key waystation for Virginia recruits heading north to the Continental Army.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.dumfriesva.gov/visitors/history.php",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A customhouse and warehouse appeared by 1731, and more followed along the estuary by 1732, fueling its port boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
